WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.890
Feeding your family well: labels, nutrients and plates.

2
00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:11.350
This is the video for Module 3 of Advanced Cooking and Nutrition: nutrition science for African families.

3
00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:20.550
Good cooking feeds the body as well as pleasing the tongue. As the cook, you decide the salt, oil and sugar in the family pot.

4
00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:28.290
You will learn which nutrients are most often missing in West African diets, and which local foods supply them.

5
00:00:29.540 --> 00:00:33.340
You will plan a week of meals using WHO healthy diet guidance.

6
00:00:34.590 --> 00:00:42.310
And you will adapt cooking for family members with diabetes or high blood pressure, always alongside their health worker's advice.

7
00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:54.220
Carbohydrates, proteins and fats give the body energy, measured in kilocalories. Carbohydrate gives 4 kcal per gram. Protein also gives 4.

8
00:00:54.570 --> 00:01:00.550
Healthy adults need about 0.83 g of protein per kilogram of body weight each day.

9
00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:18.180
Fat gives 9 kcal per gram, more than twice as much. One tablespoon of oil is about 120 kcal, so cutting two tablespoons from the family pot removes about 240 kcal. Measure your oil instead of pouring.

10
00:01:19.430 --> 00:01:33.810
For example, Grace in Lagos checks a pack of instant noodles. The label says 45 g carbohydrate, 7 g protein and 14 g fat. These are illustrative figures, so always read your own label.

11
00:01:35.060 --> 00:01:39.580
Carbohydrate: 45 times 4 is 180 kcal.

12
00:01:40.830 --> 00:01:43.930
Protein: 7 times 4 is 28 kcal.

13
00:01:45.180 --> 00:01:49.170
Fat: 14 times 9 is 126 kcal.

14
00:01:50.420 --> 00:02:03.000
The total is 334 kcal, and about 38% comes from fat. So Grace adds an egg and chopped vegetables for protein and fibre, and makes noodles an occasional food.

15
00:02:04.250 --> 00:02:19.400
Iron, vitamin A, iodine and zinc deficiencies are common, especially for women and young children. Vitamin C helps the body absorb iron from beans and greens, so serve an orange, pawpaw or guava with the meal.

16
00:02:20.650 --> 00:02:24.830
Tea and coffee reduce iron absorption, so drink them between meals.

17
00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:31.970
Wash vegetables before cutting, not after. Washing cut leaves rinses vitamins away.

18
00:02:33.220 --> 00:02:41.050
Cook leafy vegetables briefly. Do not add potash or baking soda to keep them green, because it destroys some vitamins.

19
00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:49.660
Vitamin A needs a little fat to be absorbed, and red palm oil is rich in it. Use iodised salt, stored covered.

20
00:02:50.910 --> 00:03:00.360
Use these targets for your 7-day plan. Adults need at least 400 g of fruit and vegetables a day. Yam and cassava do not count.

21
00:03:00.710 --> 00:03:08.690
Less than 5 g of salt a day, just under one level teaspoon, and seasoning cubes count. Water instead of soft drinks.

22
00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:17.870
For example, Blessing's family of five needs about 14 kg of fruit and vegetables a week, so she buys 7 kg twice a week.

23
00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:26.220
The healthy plate method: half the plate non-starchy vegetables, a quarter protein, and a quarter the starchy food.

24
00:03:27.470 --> 00:03:36.630
For many families the big change is the swallow. Measure the eba or pounded yam with a small bowl, and give more soup and vegetables instead.

25
00:03:37.880 --> 00:03:52.700
For example, Joy in Calabar cut the salt in her soup from 3 teaspoons to 1.5, and the cubes from 4 to 1. She built flavour with stock, crayfish and iru instead, and cut down gradually so tastes could adjust.

26
00:03:53.950 --> 00:03:57.220
Replace sugary drinks with water or unsweetened zobo.

27
00:03:58.470 --> 00:04:07.960
Never stop or change a prescribed medicine because the diet is working, and do not use herbal mixtures sold as cures. Keep clinic appointments.

28
00:04:09.210 --> 00:04:23.100
Do not give iron, vitamin A or other supplements on your own guesswork. Too much iron is poisonous to young children, and too much vitamin A is harmful, especially in pregnancy. Keep supplements locked away.

29
00:04:24.350 --> 00:04:34.350
If someone is always tired, has pale inner eyelids, or sees poorly in dim light, take them to a health facility. Diagnosis belongs to health workers.

30
00:04:35.600 --> 00:04:48.590
To remember. Fat carries more than twice the energy of carbs and protein. Eat vitamin C with plant iron. Aim for 400 g of fruit and vegetables and under 5 g of salt a day.

31
00:04:48.940 --> 00:04:52.590
Use the healthy plate. And never change medicines through food.

32
00:04:53.840 --> 00:05:05.490
Your practice: check three food labels, give one day of meals a micronutrient makeover, write your family's 7-day plan, and adapt one family dish with less salt and oil.

33
00:05:05.840 --> 00:05:07.780
Continue with the lessons below.
